From 19739289c33ae86f049024f7112672f4aef94a68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:37:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Launch boost: feed-forward accel when a stopped lead pulls
 away

From a dead stop the MPC answers a departing lead with a slow, jerk-limited
ramp. Drive 339 (t2_accel_cap_launch): plan peak ~1.38 m/s2, first second
of motion averages 0.6-0.7 m/s2, accel cap reached on 1 of 8 launches. Sim
sweeps showed no MPC weight, cap, floor or follow time moves this much.

New selfdrive/controls/lib/launch_boost.py (numpy only), called from
longitudinal_planner.py right after get_accel_from_plan, ACC mode only:
- arms after ego and lead have both been stopped 1 s with long active;
  latches the stop gap
- fires only when the MPC itself already asks to go (a > 0.1, so the boost
  never takes the car out of stopping on its own) and the lead is pulling
  away: filtered vLead > 0.9, aLeadK > 0.6 and the gap opened 0.4 m beyond
  the stop gap, 3 frames in a row
- boost = min(1.5*(vLead - vEgo - 0.3), 3*(gap - stop gap - 0.2 - 1.0*vEgo),
  aLeadK + 0.3), ramped at +2.5 / -1.5 m/s3, max 1.3 m/s2; the planner sends
  max(MPC, boost) before its own accel clip and clears should_stop while it
  is on
- fades out above 5 m/s, after 6 s, or once the MPC asks for as much;
  drops at once on lead lost, closer leadTwo, gap jump or shrink, lead not
  pulling away, MPC braking, crash_cnt, gas, brake, long inactive; then off
  until the car has driven off and stopped again
- while boosting, the MPC's own speed/accel state is put on the car's, so
  an abort hands the MPC the car as it is
- cloudlog "launch boost: ..." on fire / handover / abort
- live: /data/launch_boost = max boost in m/s2 (0 = off), read 1 Hz,
  clamped to [0, 1.5]; no new Params keys

Closed-loop sim (real long_mpc + real planner, which matches the harness
bit for bit; vision-like lead noise; gap0 3.5-5.5 m, lead 1.0-3.0 m/s2):
mean first-second accel 0.77 -> 1.05, v@2s 0.57 -> 0.76, v@4s 2.93 -> 3.41,
time to 5 m/s 5.64 -> 5.37 s, gap growth over 4 s 12.3 -> 11.5 m; start
of motion only 0.06 s sooner (the trigger needs ~1 s of evidence with this
noise). 0 fires in 180 noisy 60 s stops and 160 creeping-lead runs. Lead
re-braking, lead loss, leadTwo, pedals: safe, never closer than baseline
by more than ~0.7 m and never below 3.0 m.

Brake ramp: this lineage sends ACC_neg_Sollbeschl_Grad_02 = 1.0. If the
ESP honours that, the boosted car cannot shed its accel in time and a lead
that stops again 2-3 s after launching becomes unsafe in sim (baseline
fine). With the upstream 4.0 (fix_brake_ramp_4p0) it is safe. Drive this
on top of fix_brake_ramp_4p0.

